<mujoco model="H1-2 Lowerbody">
  <!-- Robot + scene model.

       h1_2_magpie.xml and its nested includes (magpie_gripper_left.xml,
       magpie_gripper.xml) are NOT committed into the submodule: they are
       bind-mounted from CL_Assets/mujoco_assets/ into this task directory at
       container start (see docker/docker-compose.yml, the `ros` service).
       h1_2_magpie.xml is a complete model (floor, lights, materials, 12+ leg/arm
       actuators); CL_Assets stays the single source of truth.

       MESH NOTE: h1_2_magpie.xml sets `compiler meshdir="../meshes"`, which —
       once inlined here — would resolve to mjpc/tasks/meshes. The <compiler>
       line below is placed AFTER the include so its meshdir wins the merge and
       re-points mesh lookup at the `meshes/` bind mount of CL_Assets/meshes
       inside THIS directory, keeping the task fully self-contained. -->

  <!-- PUSHING THE ROBOT (disturbance testing): use the native perturbation —
       double-click a body (e.g. pelvis or torso) to select it, then
       Ctrl+right-drag applies a force at the grab point, Ctrl+left-drag a
       torque; releasing the mouse ends the push. The force lasts as long as
       the drag, is applied only to the GUI simulation
       (app.cc PhysicsLoop -> ApplyForcePerturbations), and is NOT injected
       into planner rollouts — State::Set copies qpos/qvel/act only, so the
       planner discovers the shove through state feedback, like a real push.
       -->

  <!-- COST SENSORS GO IN THIS BLOCK, NOT AT THE BOTTOM. mjpc requires the
       <user> cost sensors to be the model's FIRST sensors (Task::Reset in
       mjpc/task.cc mju_error-aborts the whole process otherwise), and the
       include below contributes ~99 native sensors — so this block must stay
       ABOVE the include. user="<norm> <weight> <w_lo> <w_hi> [norm params]";
       each term's residual entries are written by
       H12Lowerbody::ResidualFn::Residual in declaration order.

       Pelvis Up: quadratic norm on (pelvis z-axis · world z) - 1, computed by
       PelvisUpResidual() from the pelvis_up framezaxis sensor below.

       Hips Above Knees / Knees Above Ankles: per-leg cosine alignment of the
       leg segments with world vertical — cos(knee->hip, +Z) - 1 for the thigh
       and cos(ankle->knee, +Z) - 1 for the shin (0 = joint directly above
       joint, -1 = segment horizontal, -2 = inverted), computed by
       HipsAboveKneesResidual() / KneesAboveAnklesResidual() from the framepos
       sensors below. Quadratic norm: graded pull toward vertical that starts
       at the first degree of lean (cos > 0 already implies "above").

       Torso Above Hips: same cosine alignment for the trunk axis —
       hips-center -> shoulders-center vs world vertical (dim 1), computed by
       TorsoAboveHipsResidual() from the hip/shoulder joint-center framepos
       sensors.

       Foot Width: signed stance margin (dim 1), computed by
       FootWidthResidual() — horizontal (xy) distance between the
       foot-geometry centers minus the allowed 0.4572 m (1.5 ft); the height
       difference is deliberately not charged. The rectify norm (8, one-sided
       softplus p=0.01) makes it an inequality: free while the feet are close
       enough, ~linear in the excess beyond.

       Foot Crossing: per-foot signed side margin (dim 2: left, right),
       computed by FootCrossingResidual() — each foot-geometry center must
       stay on its own side of the pelvis sagittal plane (pelvis y-axis
       flattened to horizontal), with a 5 cm clearance band around the
       midline. Positive when the foot crosses toward/past the midline; the
       rectify norm (one-sided softplus p=0.01) charges only that side, so a
       legal stance is free.

       Hip Parity: mirror-symmetry error between the two hips (dim 3: pitch,
       roll, yaw), computed by HipParityResidual() from the jointpos sensors
       below. Both sides' hip joints share identical axes (yaw +z, pitch +y,
       roll +x), so a sagittally mirrored pose has equal pitches and OPPOSITE
       rolls/yaws (the mirrored roll ranges confirm the convention):
       residuals are qL - qR for pitch and qL + qR for roll/yaw. Quadratic
       norm — keeps the legs doing the same thing without pinning them to a
       particular pose.

       Hip Yaw Zero: the hip yaw angles themselves (dim 2: left, right),
       computed by HipYawZeroResidual() from the *_hip_yaw_q sensors — pulls
       both toes to point straight forward. Complements Hip Parity, whose yaw
       entry (yawL + yawR) is blind to mirrored toe-out/toe-in. Quadratic
       norm.

       Hip Roll Zero: the hip roll angles themselves (dim 2: left, right),
       computed by HipRollZeroResidual() from the *_hip_roll_q sensors —
       pulls the legs to hang straight down rather than splayed/adducted.
       Complements Hip Parity, whose roll entry (rollL + rollR) is blind to
       mirrored splay. Quadratic norm.

       Height: signed height deficit (dim 1), computed by HeightResidual() —
       1.0 m minus the pelvis height ABOVE THE LOWER FOOT-GEOMETRY CENTER
       (+ its nominal 0.0468 m ground clearance, so it reads as
       height-above-ground on flat stance; default standing pelvis is
       1.03 m). Kinematic rather than world z, so the same residual is
       observable on the real robot from encoders + IMU. The rectify norm
       (8, one-sided softplus p=0.01) makes it an inequality: free while
       above 1 m, ~linear in every meter below.

       COM_Projection: ||capture_point_xy - support_center_xy|| (scalar),
       computed by CoMProjectionResidual(). Capture point = whole-robot CoM
       projected by the live LIPM constant sqrt(h / g), with h the CoM height
       above the lower foot-geometry center (kinematically observable — no
       absolute world z); support center =
       mean of the two FOOT-GEOMETRY centers (ankle_roll origins offset
       +3.3 cm along each foot's forward axis — the ankle joints sit behind
       the foot center). SmoothAbs norm p=0.1. Descended from humanoid-stand's
       "Balance"; dims below are translated to this robot (nv=45). The
       velocity projection doubles as the damping term (there is deliberately
       no separate CoM-velocity cost).

       Joint Vel.: qvel[6:] (all 39 non-root DOFs, incl. the passive gripper
       linkage), computed by JointVelResidual(). Quadratic, small weight —
       kills sampling-noise flail.

       JointTorques: per-actuator torque (actuator_force — these are gear=1
       torque motors, so this is the ctrlrange-clamped ctrl) normalized by
       the capacity max(|ctrlrange|), computed by JointTorquesResidual() —
       each entry is the fraction of available torque in use. All 31
       actuators, not just the legs: the frozen arm/gripper motors get a
       gradient to stop fighting the freeze equalities. Quadratic, small
       weight — the control-effort regularizer that conditions iLQG and
       kills chattery torques. -->
  <sensor>
    <user name="Pelvis Up" dim="1" user="0 1.0 0.0 10.0"/>
    <user name="Hips Above Knees" dim="2" user="0 1.0 0.0 10.0"/>
    <user name="Knees Above Ankles" dim="2" user="0 1.0 0.0 10.0"/>
    <user name="Torso Above Hips" dim="1" user="0 1.0 0.0 10.0"/>
    <user name="Foot Width" dim="1" user="8 1.0 0.0 10.0 0.01"/>
    <user name="Foot Crossing" dim="2" user="8 1.0 0.0 10.0 0.01"/>
    <user name="Hip Parity" dim="3" user="0 1.0 0.0 10.0"/>
    <user name="Hip Yaw Zero" dim="2" user="0 1.0 0.0 10.0"/>
    <user name="Hip Roll Zero" dim="2" user="0 1.0 0.0 10.0"/>
    <user name="Height" dim="1" user="8 1.0 0.0 10.0 0.01"/>
    <user name="COM_Projection" dim="1" user="6 50.0 0.0 100.0 0.1"/>
    <user name="Joint Vel." dim="39" user="0 0.01 0.0 0.1"/>
    <user name="JointTorques" dim="31" user="0 0.01 0.0 0.1"/>

    <!-- Residual inputs (native sensors; must come AFTER the <user> terms).
         objtype MUST be "xbody" (the body frame): "body" would attach to the
         INERTIAL frame, whose principal axes are arbitrarily rotated. The leg
         link body-frame origins sit exactly at their joint centers. -->
    <framezaxis name="pelvis_up" objtype="xbody" objname="pelvis"/>
    <!-- Pelvis origin + y-axis (leftward) for the Foot Crossing sagittal
         plane. -->
    <framepos name="pelvis_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="pelvis"/>
    <frameyaxis name="pelvis_yaxis" objtype="xbody" objname="pelvis"/>
    <!-- Whole-robot CoM: pelvis is the kinematic root, so its subtree is the
         entire robot. com_position is unused by the costs so far but feeds
         GUI traces and the upcoming Balance (CoM-over-feet) term. -->
    <subtreecom name="com_position" body="pelvis"/>
    <subtreelinvel name="com_velocity" body="pelvis"/>
    <framepos name="left_hip_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="left_hip_pitch_link"/>
    <framepos name="right_hip_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="right_hip_pitch_link"/>
    <framepos name="left_shoulder_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="left_shoulder_pitch_link"/>
    <framepos name="right_shoulder_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="right_shoulder_pitch_link"/>
    <framepos name="left_knee_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="left_knee_link"/>
    <framepos name="right_knee_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="right_knee_link"/>
    <framepos name="left_ankle_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="left_ankle_pitch_link"/>
    <framepos name="right_ankle_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="right_ankle_pitch_link"/>
    <!-- Foot (sole) bodies for the COM_Projection support average; the
         x-axes carry the ankle->foot-center offset direction. -->
    <framepos name="left_foot_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="left_ankle_roll_link"/>
    <framepos name="right_foot_pos" objtype="xbody" objname="right_ankle_roll_link"/>
    <framexaxis name="left_foot_xaxis" objtype="xbody" objname="left_ankle_roll_link"/>
    <framexaxis name="right_foot_xaxis" objtype="xbody" objname="right_ankle_roll_link"/>
    <!-- Hip joint angles for the Hip Parity mirror-symmetry term. -->
    <jointpos name="left_hip_pitch_q" joint="left_hip_pitch_joint"/>
    <jointpos name="right_hip_pitch_q" joint="right_hip_pitch_joint"/>
    <jointpos name="left_hip_roll_q" joint="left_hip_roll_joint"/>
    <jointpos name="right_hip_roll_q" joint="right_hip_roll_joint"/>
    <jointpos name="left_hip_yaw_q" joint="left_hip_yaw_joint"/>
    <jointpos name="right_hip_yaw_q" joint="right_hip_yaw_joint"/>
  </sensor>

  <include file="h1_2_magpie.xml"/>
  <compiler meshdir="meshes"/>

  <!-- FREEZE everything above the hips: equality-lock the waist, both arms,
       and the gripper drive hinges, leaving only the two legs (+ floating
       base) free. With joint2 omitted the constraint is
       q - qpos0 = polycoef[0], and this model has no keyframes and no joint
       ref offsets (qpos0 = 0), so every joint is pinned at the zero reference
       pose. The passive gripper hinges (*_hinge_2/3) are deliberately NOT
       pinned — the four-bar <connect> equalities in h1_2_magpie.xml already
       close them, and locking the drive hinge fixes the whole linkage;
       pinning them too would over-constrain it. The planner still samples the
       frozen joints' actuators (wasted dims — the constraints win); remove
       the actuators via a model variant if that becomes a throughput problem.
       To unfreeze at runtime (e.g. per mode), toggle data->eq_active by
       equality name. -->
  <equality>
    <joint name="freeze_torso" joint1="torso_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>

    <joint name="freeze_left_shoulder_pitch" joint1="left_shoulder_pitch_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_shoulder_roll" joint1="left_shoulder_roll_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_shoulder_yaw" joint1="left_shoulder_yaw_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_elbow" joint1="left_elbow_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_wrist_roll" joint1="left_wrist_roll_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_wrist_pitch" joint1="left_wrist_pitch_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_wrist_yaw" joint1="left_wrist_yaw_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>

    <joint name="freeze_right_shoulder_pitch" joint1="right_shoulder_pitch_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_right_shoulder_roll" joint1="right_shoulder_roll_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_right_shoulder_yaw" joint1="right_shoulder_yaw_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_right_elbow" joint1="right_elbow_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_right_wrist_roll" joint1="right_wrist_roll_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_right_wrist_pitch" joint1="right_wrist_pitch_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_right_wrist_yaw" joint1="right_wrist_yaw_joint" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>

    <!-- Gripper drive hinges ("left/right" in hinge names = finger side;
         leftg_* = left hand). -->
    <joint name="freeze_right_hand_left_finger" joint1="left_hinge_1" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_right_hand_right_finger" joint1="right_hinge_1" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_hand_left_finger" joint1="leftg_left_hinge_1" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
    <joint name="freeze_left_hand_right_finger" joint1="leftg_right_hinge_1" polycoef="0 0 0 0 0"/>
  </equality>

  <!-- Arena sized for contact-rich states: a fallen/tangled robot makes 100+
       contacts and the constraint solve overruns 1M (mj_stackAlloc abort). -->
  <size memory="10M"/>

  <!-- MJPC planner defaults. Tune as the lower-body controller is implemented.
       agent_planner 2 = iLQG (enum PlannerType in mjpc/planners/include.h);
       the sampling_* numerics below only take effect if the planner is
       switched back to Sampling (0) in the GUI. -->
  <custom>
    <numeric name="agent_planner" data="2" />
    <numeric name="agent_horizon" data="0.35" />
    <numeric name="agent_timestep" data="0.01" />
    <numeric name="sampling_trajectories" data="60" />
    <numeric name="sampling_spline_points" data="3" />
    <numeric name="sampling_exploration" data="0.1" />
  </custom>

  <!-- Cost terms: one mjpc <user> sensor per residual term, in the <sensor>
       block ABOVE the include (ordering constraint documented there). -->
</mujoco>
